{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.HeckeStrands","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.HeckeStrands","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.RibbonDH","lean:module:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.heckeMonodromy_shadow_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.heckeMonodromy_shadow_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/HeckeStrands.lean#L93-L105","doc":"**At fixed `ℏ` the shadow is zero.** Since `q = e^{iπℏ} ≠ 1` for transcendental `ℏ`\n(`qV_sub_inv_ne_zero`), a tower whose monodromy factors through `D_ℏ` has only the zero ring as a\n`q ↦ 1` shadow (`subsingleton_of_fixed_coupling`). The classical shadow is a statement about the\nfamily over the coupling, not about one `D_ℏ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.heckeMonodromy_of_DH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.heckeMonodromy_of_DH","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/HeckeStrands.lean#L77-L90","doc":"**Step 2 from Drinfeld–Kohno alone.** For a Markov-trace tower over a commutative ring `R`,\nwith `q : Rˣ` mapped to `q = e^{iπℏ}` by `φ : R → ℂ`, whose generators are the images of the\n`D_ℏ` braid generators (`BraidedMonodromy`), the step-2 class holds for any shadow `ε` lying over\n`q ↦ 1`. By `heckeMonodromy_shadow_trivial` that shadow is necessarily zero when the monodromy\nfactors through `D_ℏ` at one fixed `ℏ`: the shadow needs the family in `ℏ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.far_strand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.far_strand","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/HeckeStrands.lean#L70-L74","doc":"**Far commutation on every `V^{⊗n}`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.braid_strand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.braid_strand","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/HeckeStrands.lean#L63-L68","doc":"**Braid relation on every `V^{⊗n}`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.hecke_strand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.hecke_strand","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/HeckeStrands.lean#L57-L61","doc":"**Hecke quadratic on every strand of `V^{⊗n}`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.g_isYB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.g_isYB","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/HeckeStrands.lean#L53-L55","doc":"`g` satisfies the three-strand (Yang–Baxter) relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.g_quad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.g_quad","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/HeckeStrands.lean#L43-L51","doc":"**The Hecke quadratic on two strands** in `D_ℏ`: `g² = (q − q⁻¹) g + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.gDH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.Drinfeld.gDH","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/Drinfeld/HeckeStrands.lean#L40-L41","doc":"The rescaled braiding `g = s · β_{V,V}`, `s = e^{iπℏ/2}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}